This unofficial package downloads Fish Speech and the S2-Pro model from
their original publishers. It does not include their binaries or weights
in its installer ZIP and is not endorsed by Fish Audio.

The portable wrapper changes runtime behavior by limiting the text model's
context to 4096 by default, disabling torch.compile, and splitting long
single-speaker input into independent short requests. It does not modify
the downloaded source files or checkpoint files.

The wrapper also constructs text-model parameters on the meta device
before the upstream assign=True checkpoint load, avoiding a redundant
random FP32 copy in RAM. Nonpersistent buffers are materialized on CPU.

